{
  "id": "wulfic-stage-ab-reset-alphabets",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Restarted alphabets at five LP2 boundaries",
  "question": "Would a shared substitution alphabet at each position after a section, paragraph, clause, line or page restart leave more same-position repeats than LP2 shows?",
  "reader_question": "Could the key restart on each page or line?",
  "summary": "A pinned public source test of five restart boundaries was reproduced byte-for-byte; LP2 same-position repeats fall below both planted-control ranges under its exact model.",
  "finding": "Across 12,956 runes and five boundary types, LP2 repeats stayed near flat-rune expectations and below the conservative bound from both planted plaintext sources. The 1,000-null and 200-per-source-control run reproduced the public result and control tables byte-for-byte.",
  "limitations": "This tests Wulfic Stage AB’s shared, position-dependent substitution alphabets with its anti-doublet postprocessing and two plaintext controls. It does not exclude every page- or line-reset cipher, feedback rule, other plaintext distribution, or independently chosen alphabet per unit.",
  "next_steps": "A new reset model should specify how state restarts and demonstrate that planted outputs under that model are distinguishable before evaluating LP2.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
  "tags": [
